## Prompt 2 — Replace positional slices with relevance ranking

```
This function selects events to send to an LLM by taking the first N items from a
filtered list. There is no scoring or sorting, so which events survive is arbitrary —
it depends on list order, not importance. On long runs the causally significant events
fall outside the window.

Replace every first-N slice with a ranked best-N selection:

1. Add a scoring function that ranks each event by a weighted combination of:
   - whether the error was unrecovered vs. later retried/resolved
   - temporal proximity to the first failure or terminal event
   - how central the emitting component is to the flow being analyzed
   - rarity of the message pattern (repeated identical noise scores lower)
2. Sort by score descending, then take the top N.
3. Make the weights module-level named constants with a comment explaining each.
4. Keep the same N so this change is isolated and measurable on its own.
5. Log the score distribution of selected vs. dropped events so selection is inspectable.

Add unit tests that assert a high-signal event placed at the end of a long input list
still gets selected. Show the diff and tests.
```

