## Prompt 3 — Tail-preserving message truncation

```
This code truncates log messages with a head slice, keeping only the first N characters.
For stack traces and nested error payloads the actual cause is at the END of the string,
so head truncation systematically discards the most diagnostic part.

Replace it with a helper that preserves both ends:
- keep the first ~60% of the budget
- keep the last ~40%
- join with a clear elision marker showing how many characters were dropped
- if the message is under the budget, return it unchanged

Apply this helper everywhere messages are truncated before being sent to the LLM.
Add unit tests covering: under-budget passthrough, exact-budget boundary, and a long
string where a marker at the very end must survive. Show the diff and tests.
```

