## Prompt 4 — Contract consistency between finding type and finding body

```
In this code, a categorical "finding type" field is set to its strongest value based
purely on overall status, without checking that the corresponding finding text was
actually produced. So the output can claim it has a root cause while the root cause
field is empty.

Downstream consumers gate their rendering on the text field being non-empty, so these
records render as nothing at all — a failed run with no explanation shown.

Fix the contract so the two fields cannot disagree:
1. Only assign the strongest finding type when the finding text is actually present.
2. When status indicates failure but no finding text was produced, emit an explicit
   "undetermined" state carrying a short machine-readable reason.
3. Add a validator on the model that rejects the inconsistent combination outright.
4. Add tests for: failure with text, failure without text, and success without text.

Show the diff and tests.
```

