## Prompt 8 — Deduplicate a repeated UI block

```
The same semantic element is implemented three separate times across this codebase, in
three different styling approaches — one utility-class-first, one mixed, one inline-style
first. Only one of the three applies text formatting for readability, so identical content
renders well in one place and as an unbroken block in the others.

Extract a single shared component that:
- takes the finding text, the finding type, and a confidence level as props
- applies the readability formatting in all cases
- uses design tokens only, no hardcoded color values
- handles the empty and low-confidence states from the previous prompt

Replace all three call sites with it. Show the new component and the three diffs.
```

