## Suggested order

Run 1 first and measure before doing anything else — it is one line and may account for
a large share of the error. Then 2, 3, 6 (all contained and independently testable),
then 4 and 7 together, then 5, then 8.

Measure accuracy on a fixed benchmark set after each step so you know which change
actually moved the number.

## A note on the target

Expect a well-tuned version of this to land in the high-80s to low-90s on clear-signal
cases, not 100%. Some inputs have genuinely ambiguous evidence and some have no causal
signal present at all. The more valuable goal is calibration: be right most of the time
and reliably know when you are not, so that uncertain results are labeled rather than
asserted. Prompt 5 is what buys that.
